{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1517617-well-i-tried-wraith","id":1517617,"title":"Well, I tried Wraith","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-09T19:00:28-07:00","id":1517617,"title":"Well, I tried Wraith","content":"I got Wraith, a friend gave me the book. like two decades ago. I read most of it; it didn't really stick. I mean, the art is good, the writings are all the same as the other books. But it never really stuck with me. We like the movie, <i>the Crow</i> and <i>Risen</i> is an awesome book, but, it's just not interesting; perhaps just my personal-tastes. (And I feel the same way about <i>Changeling, the Dreaming</i>, even though it's a lot like<i> Ars Magica</i>).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T19:21:12-07:00","id":1517619,"title":"","content":"Annnnnnnnnnnnd?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T18:52:57-07:00","id":1518118,"title":"","content":"What exactly would you like us to tell you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-16T03:08:19-07:00","id":1518137,"title":"","content":"So for me there\u2019s a difference between using a setting and playing a setting.<br /> <br /> In 30+ years we\u2019ve never played a Wraith or Changeling campaign, however both are integral parts of our campaign mythology (Changeling with some heavy tweaking).<br /> <br /> From the time they were published we incorporated them alongside our own ideas, the shadowlands sit alongside the other two penumbras and the near dreaming on top of material reality.<br /> <br /> In our recent campaign both have taken a more prominent role, our Mage is Fey blooded with a Dreaming minor sphere so constantly interacts with the Dreaming, whilst due to currently being set in Victorian London the presence of the dead and popularity of spiritualism provides a dark backdrop from the shadowlands.<br /> <br /> So you might not want to play the settings but they can certainly add flavour or background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-17T00:40:25-07:00","id":1518170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1517617-well-i-tried-wraith#post1517617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> perhaps just my personal-tastes</div> </div> </div> </div>Tastes differ<br /> The characters are constantly at war with themselves (and sometimes each other) while trying to find their place in both life and death. Not to mention, you start as... a faluire. You've failed to pass on to the true afterlife, and your soul has ended up in the Shadowlands, a decaying spiritual reflection of the real world. You're bound to this side of reality by your Fetters and Passions. You have to negotiate the viper's nest of politics that's been set up in the Shadowlands \u2014 a three-way clusterfuck between the oppressive Hierarchy, the revolutionary Renegades, and the devout Heretics \u2014 while trying to protect and, eventually, resolve that which ties you to this life and move on to the <i>true afterlife.</i><br /> It considered by many to be one of if not the most depressing of the World of Darkness games<br /> Yet...<br /> Yet Wraith: The Oblivion weirdly is <b>the most hopeful of the settings </b>in the World of Darkness!<br /> Managing to resolve your fetters and passions, thus ascending out of the Shadowlands is a very attainable goal, putting it way ahead of the all but impossible existential goals from Vampire and Werewolf, the at-the-very-least highly unlikely goals of Mage, or the no-kidding-you're-screwed-no-way-out nihilism of Changeling...<br /> <br /> And as Arcanus said, there\u2019s a difference between using a setting and playing a setting.<br /> Wraith is not needed, but good to have around<br /> It gives and adds a little umph to the stories - but this is true to basically any other setting, there existence and incorporation will enrich your games<br /> But if its not your cup of tea? No problem, just ignore it<br /> You tried, and not liked it.<br /> Happens <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 07-17-2023, 03:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T21:03:41-07:00","id":1518807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1517617-well-i-tried-wraith?p=1518170#post1518170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And as Arcanus said, there\u2019s a difference between using a setting and playing a setting.<br /> Wraith is not needed, but good to have around<br /> It gives and adds a little umph to the stories - but this is true to basically any other setting, there existence and incorporation will enrich your games<br /> But if its not your cup of tea? No problem, just ignore it<br /> You tried, and not liked it.<br /> Happens <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The best use I've found for Wraith to have around is for V:tM players that like their Dark Fate flaw; when they reach Final-Death, they are auto-Wraithed. <br /> <br /> Wraith would be great for a Crow type game, but, I'd have to understand the interactions of the dead more. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T21:47:30-07:00","id":1518809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1517617-well-i-tried-wraith?p=1518807#post1518807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">their Dark Fate flaw; when they reach Final-Death, they are auto-Wraithed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The irony is, that isn't a &quot;Dark Fate&quot; per se, but technically a Second Chance <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> a Final Death is... well.. Final; the Vampire is &quot;gone&quot; (except when not... but that is a different matter), for a Vampire to become a Wraith and potentially reach the True Afterlife (tm) ? Even with the whole insanity of the Underworld politics and intrigues and dangers thats is something no vampire (amybe not even those who reached Golconda) could hope for<br /> I would hug my ST if she would make my vampire a Wraith after it kicked the bucket <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T12:15:54-07:00","id":1518838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1517617-well-i-tried-wraith?p=1518170#post1518170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yet Wraith: The Oblivion weirdly is <b>the most hopeful of the settings </b>in the World of Darkness!<br /> Managing to resolve your fetters and passions, thus ascending out of the Shadowlands is a very attainable goal, putting it way ahead of the all but impossible existential goals from Vampire and Werewolf, the at-the-very-least highly unlikely goals of Mage, or the no-kidding-you're-screwed-no-way-out nihilism of Changeling...<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> this always sounded to me more like a talking point about the setting than an accurate description of the situation, like &quot;changeling is the darkest wod game&quot;.<br /> <br /> Wraith was never really set on whenethere transcendance was achievable the classical way if you fetters were destroyed before being resolved.<br /> <br /> As for the others, their goals are not that hard. Golconda can be achieved with a similar difficulty as transcendance. The method is close to the same, and once achieved, only stupidity can lead you out of golconda.<br /> <br /> Garou can stop the apocalypse, they have the tools at their disposal and any motivated and knowledgable pack can punch the wyrm in the balls by killing the maeljin.<br /> The only reason it's werewolf &quot;the apocalypse&quot; is because the writers made generations of garou NPCs dumb as malfeas.<br /> Achieving personal ascension is also similar to golconda and transcendance in term of personal journey. Even an apprentice can attain it. And changing the consensus is really just a matter of using vulgar magic in front of the public and carefully dealing with the risks of paradox. Which aren't that high.<br /> <br /> As for changeling, while the books like to claims their are screwed, that statement is never justified in setting, as inspiration is not that hard to do, art can be created. And there's a secret i thr deep dreaming that, if resolved, will &quot;usher a new age of spring&quot;.<br /> <br /> So if we take into account everything, wraith re indeed in the worst position<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T01:24:07-07:00","id":1518884,"title":"","content":"let's agree to disagree<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1517617-well-i-tried-wraith?p=1518838#post1518838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for the others, their goals are not that hard.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's agree to disagree, shall we? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1517617-well-i-tried-wraith?p=1518838#post1518838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Golconda can be achieved with a similar difficulty as transcendance.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> I would argue tho' Golconda is NOT the goal of Vampire<br /> Vampire have several goals, Golconda could be one of them, thats true, but even Golconda wouldn't save you from Gehenna<br /> To become an Elder is not just survival, you literally have to eat your way up to the foodchain if you are not strong in generation enough to have enough thick blood, but most of the Vampire chornicles are not about golconda nor about to become an Elder, but to survive long anough untill you ultimately eaten by something stronger<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1517617-well-i-tried-wraith?p=1518838#post1518838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Garou can stop the apocalypse, they have the tools at their disposal and any motivated and knowledgable pack can punch the wyrm in the balls by killing the maeljin.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bLet's agree to disagree on that too, shall we? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> The Garou in theory maybe have everything to achive their goals (tho' goals varied to Tribe to tribe, sept to sept, even pack to pack) but on the similar note Humanity have everything to have World Peace \u200b, yet just how the Garou failed through History to &quot;Win&quot;, smiilarly Humanity not managed to put aside differences and work for a better world, yet we had and have everything to do it<br /> Again, in a chronicel, you probably will die as a hero, but will not prevent the apocalypse nor stop/rehabilitate the Wyrm or Weaver<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1517617-well-i-tried-wraith?p=1518838#post1518838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for changeling, while the books like to claims their are screwed, that statement is never justified in setting, as inspiration is not that hard to do, art can be created. And there's a secret i thr deep dreaming that, if resolved, will &quot;usher a new age of spring&quot;.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The book claims... because they ARE<br /> And the setting justified it too, and yes, art could be created, inspiration is possible, but every passing day Winter is closer, the cold and harsh reality, Banality, a force representing the loss of humanity's capacity to dream and believe in magic, slowly kills you...<br /> It doesn't help that the game line itself has so many ways to go, you have little idea what the authors want\u2014a fable on the death of childhood innocence? A game of raging against the dying of the light? An urban fantasy game about balancing the fantastic and the mundane? The commonly derided &quot;bear and balloons&quot; illustration near the start of the 2nd edition core book didn't exactly help matters.\u200b<br /> You and your friends try to survive, eke out an existence trying to bring Glamour and magic back into the world....<br /> ...yet it was the moon landing in 1969, not Woodstock, which brought about such a surge of Glamour that it threw open the closed Gates of Arcadia, if only for a moment, and allowed the disappeared fairy nobility, the sidhe, to re-enter the world of mortals.<br /> Where they were stuck in mortal bodies afterwards.<br /> The changeling &quot;task&quot; and plans to survive and reignite Humanity's capacity to dream and believe in magic is practically impossible<br /> It is helluva depressing setting in my opinion, but as I said, let's agree to disagree!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T12:31:34-07:00","id":1518951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1517617-well-i-tried-wraith?p=1518884#post1518884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">let's agree to disagree<br /> <br /> <br /> I would argue tho' Golconda is NOT the goal of Vampire</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Without trying to sound agressive, but saying &quot;let's agree to disagree&quot; before arguing back sends a weirdly mixed signal.<br /> &quot;Let's agree to disagree&quot; implies a desire to not take part in a debate or end a debate. Arguing back implies the opposite. So I'm really not sure of what you want.<br /> <br /> One could argue as well that transcendance is not the goal of wraith, since most wraiths don't care about it nor act toward it. Trying to push back oblivion to exist forever as a wraith, trying to escape the underworld toward the skinland or the umbra or shattering the veil are also goals of wraiths. Whule there's more wraiths pursuing transcendance than vampire (openly) pursuing golconda, it isn't a common quest of wraith societies.<br /> <br /> you could say that transcendance was stated as the one hope of all wraiths in at least the 1st edition. But the same was said in vtm 1st ed, which precise that all vampires, if they live long enough, will either seek balance through golconda or to become human again. And like further editions of vtm, the second edition of wraith took steps afar from that, with transcendance being a rare occurence seen as a myth by most.<br /> <br /> Same thing with personal ascension, which was stated as the main goal of most mage and not that impossible to get, with even a relatively step by step way described in the 2nd edition corebook, and then from there the game made it more innefable and so rare that it's basically a legend in revised.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1517617-well-i-tried-wraith?p=1518884#post1518884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire have several goals, Golconda could be one of them, thats true, but even Golconda wouldn't save you from Gehenna</div> </div> </div> </div>It does saves you from gehenna. You're already saved. If you die while in golconda, you'll never become a wraith, and you can't ever be diablerised.<br /> So what is the problem with gehenna coming? At worst, you'll die and go to the true afterlife. <br /> <br /> A vampire in golconda waiting for gehenna is like a solo video game player who already 100% the game and is just chilling around the game world before inevitably leaving.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1517617-well-i-tried-wraith?p=1518884#post1518884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To become an Elder is not just survival, you literally have to eat your way up to the foodchain if you are not strong in generation enough to have enough thick blood, but most of the Vampire chornicles are not about golconda nor about to become an Elder, but to survive long anough untill you ultimately eaten by something stronger<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's not true in the absolute. Unless you're under heavy dominate or a blood bond, nothing forces a vampire to exist in a city where the jyhad put everyone against each others.<br /> <br /> Half the gangrel lives that way, as do all autarkis or anyone who avieve golconda. Unless you actively desires to kill the primogen or to be prince, nothing forbid you from blood bonding/dominating/presencing/straight out pay a mortal to drive you in their car to the closest village/small town with no other vampires to clash with you.<br /> <br /> You play the jyhad because you want something that only fighting for power can give you, not because it's an inavoidable part of one's vampiric nature. Vampires needs only two things to survive, blood and a place to hide during the day. Neither of which requires byzantine political manoevers.<br /> <br /> The reason why most vampires play the jyhad is because they either refuse to abandon the power they gained or never thought about escaping.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1517617-well-i-tried-wraith?p=1518884#post1518884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bLet's agree to disagree on that too, shall we? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> The Garou in theory maybe have everything to achive their goals (tho' goals varied to Tribe to tribe, sept to sept, even pack to pack) but on the similar note Humanity have everything to have World Peace \u200b, yet just how the Garou failed through History to &quot;Win&quot;, smiilarly Humanity not managed to put aside differences and work for a better world, yet we had and have everything to do it<br /> Again, in a chronicel, you probably will die as a hero, but will not prevent the apocalypse nor stop/rehabilitate the Wyrm or Weaver<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Garou failed because the writers wanted to have an apocalypse, not because it was the logical devellopment of their culture/flaws and capabilities.<br /> <br /> world peace for humans can only be achieved if deep seated instincts ,the potentially inevitable tribalism of our species and scarcity of ressources can be overcome, which we don't know of it is even possible.<br /> <br /> The garou don't have such limitation. They are build to punch cthulhu in the guts, and the wyrm can be twarted by doing exactly that, with each maeljin being killable, and each wyrm cult, including pentex, being mortal.<br /> <br /> The only reason pentex and co are still existing is because they have plot armor. No company would survives having it's employee systematically rampage and it's operations ruined beyond hope.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1517617-well-i-tried-wraith?p=1518884#post1518884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book claims... because they ARE<br /> And the setting justified it too, and yes, art could be created, inspiration is possible, but every passing day Winter is closer, the cold and harsh reality, Banality, a force representing the loss of humanity's capacity to dream and believe in magic, slowly kills you...<br /> It doesn't help that the game line itself has so many ways to go, you have little idea what the authors want\u2014a fable on the death of childhood innocence? A game of raging against the dying of the light? An urban fantasy game about balancing the fantastic and the mundane? The commonly derided &quot;bear and balloons&quot; illustration near the start of the 2nd edition core book didn't exactly help matters.\u200b<br /> You and your friends try to survive, eke out an existence trying to bring Glamour and magic back into the world....<br /> ...yet it was the moon landing in 1969, not Woodstock, which brought about such a surge of Glamour that it threw open the closed Gates of Arcadia, if only for a moment, and allowed the disappeared fairy nobility, the sidhe, to re-enter the world of mortals.<br /> Where they were stuck in mortal bodies afterwards.<br /> The changeling &quot;task&quot; and plans to survive and reignite Humanity's capacity to dream and believe in magic is practically impossible<br /> It is helluva depressing setting in my opinion, but as I said, let's agree to disagree!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And the claims of the books are contradicted by both the system, most of the lore and it's willingness to be set inside the modern era on earth.<br /> <br /> As you said, the author didn't agreed on what they wanted with changeling. Which explain why it is deeply incoherent.<br /> <br /> For exemple, there's zero explaination for why an endless winter would ever come, why banality would be stronger than creativity than in previous era when we're factually more creative than in any time of history, simply due to the ability to exchange concepts daily and societies than, for the most part of them, value creativity and individual acts of art creation more than in previous eras. <br /> <br /> <br /> Surviving in changeling, if one takes account of both the rules and the metaphysics, surviving as a changeling is no harder than for a vampire. You just have to live close to creative people/industries and use your arts to cut away all ways their creativity could be limited by real life.<br /> <br /> <br /> It doesn't helps that there's hardly a valid justification for why running away to the deep dreaming isn't an option. The place is protected from banality by it's very nature, shows no sign of suffering from impact from the waking world, and going there is relatively easy.<br /> <br /> Bedlam clearly is an ad hoc justication of the authors who realised &quot;oh shit, if we don't add something, nothing stop the players from avoiding all changeling-in-the-modern-world issues by running away in the far dreaming or staying next to their balor's fire ad vitam.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A common issue of the desired themes and ways of playing the wod games is that it only works if the players and by extention their characters decide to be a certain way rather than act logically.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T19:44:28-07:00","id":1519308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1517617-well-i-tried-wraith?p=1518809#post1518809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The irony is, that isn't a &quot;Dark Fate&quot; per se, but technically a Second Chance <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> a Final Death is... well.. Final; the Vampire is &quot;gone&quot; (except when not... but that is a different matter), for a Vampire to become a Wraith and potentially reach the True Afterlife (tm) ? Even with the whole insanity of the Underworld politics and intrigues and dangers thats is something no vampire (amybe not even those who reached Golconda) could hope for<br /> I would hug my ST if she would make my vampire a Wraith after it kicked the bucket <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Our games are very lethal and players are used to rolling up new characters, but, Dark-Fate keeps them in vampire-game and prevents them from making a new blood-sucker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T09:09:46-07:00","id":1523425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1517617-well-i-tried-wraith#post1517617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got Wraith, a friend gave me the book. like two decades ago. I read most of it; it didn't really stick. I mean, the art is good, the writings are all the same as the other books. But it never really stuck with me. We like the movie, <i>the Crow</i> and <i>Risen</i> is an awesome book, but, it's just not interesting; perhaps just my personal-tastes. (And I feel the same way about <i>Changeling, the Dreaming</i>, even though it's a lot like<i> Ars Magica</i>).</div> </div> </div> </div>But you haven't really played it?<br /> <br /> You should give it a try. WtO is my second favorite after MtA.<br /> <br /> But hey, to each their own. Personal tastes are... Personal, after all. If you don't like, you don't like it, that's fine.<br /> <br /> I love it, I find the entire setting fascinating, so I would always recommend people to give it a try, maybe you'll change your mind, but if you don't, that's fine, just play what is more attuned to your tastes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}